=== PREFLIGHT ===
Predecessors: P3-0001 UI (cf1190cb), P1 facade (43d600e5), P2 tokens (b40c9d6b). Clean-tree: apps/apple/Sources/Components/{Feedback,Forms}/** + tests.

=== SURVEY ===
Mapped web `components/feedback` + `forms`. Reused tokens + P3-0001 UI (TSCard/TSButton/TSBadge/TSDatePickerBridge/
TSRangeSlider) + P3-0003 (TSMetricBar/TSInlineCallout). EmptyState→ContentUnavailableView; skeletons→redacted shimmer.

=== REASONING ===
- DRY banners: TSAlertBanner base (tone/icon/title/message/action/dismiss); the 12 named banners (Offline,
  LiveStaleData, TeslaReauth, RateLimit, Maintenance, Impersonation, DraftRecovery/Restore, EditConflict,
  TimeMachine, CookieConsent, BrowserCompat) are thin presets — every web export maps to a named component.
- Error boundaries: SwiftUI has no render-time catch, so TSErrorBoundary/Section/Page render a fallback when the
  caller supplies hasError (honest equivalent, not a fake try/catch). Take no FacadeError (stays non-Shared).
- Reduce Motion: skeleton shimmer, TSTopProgress, achievement toast gate animation on accessibilityReduceMotion.
- Forms stay non-Shared: TSUnitInput is a plain numeric+unit-label input (SI conversion is the page's job via the
  facade), TSVehicleSelect/Multi are generic over (id, localized label, searchText) → fully typechecked.
- Combobox/Multi: real popover with TSSearchInput + filtered list + selection; TreeSelect over native List(children:).
- All visible strings are LocalizedStringKey (catalog-resolved); inputs carry accessibility labels/traits.

